      "title": "Apps and host",
      "items": [
        "Web is apps/web (Next.js 16). Mobile is apps/mobile (Expo 54). Package manager is Bun.",
        "Vercel preview of integration is https://preview.tempoflow.dev (docs/ENVIRONMENTS.md). Production hostname: UNKNOWN.",
        "Polar checkout route sets server to sandbox."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Convex deployments",
      "items": [
        "Registry: dev tremendous-bass-443, staging ceaseless-dog-617, prod precious-wildcat-890.",
        "Workflows call ceaseless-dog-617 the test deployment. ENVIRONMENTS.md also allows a personal dev slug.",
        "convex-deploy-test pushes integration convex/ to the test deployment. Live prod deploys are Amit only."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "AI slots",
      "items": [
        "convex/lib/ai_router.ts calls https://api.mistral.ai/v1/chat/completions with native fetch.",
        "Slots: fast mistral-small-latest, balanced mistral-medium-latest, deep mistral-large-latest.",
        "TRD section 3 still names OpenRouter and Gemma. That is not what this router calls."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Trust boundary",
      "items": [
        "People, Vercel, Polar, Mistral, and RevenueCat sit outside the Convex security group.",
        "Convex Auth, functions, and data sit inside it. The RevenueCat webhook is the crossing into Convex.",
        "Web checkout calls Polar from the Next.js route. The access token stays in server env."
      ]
    }
  ]
